# One ANCHORED POSIX-extended-regex pattern per line (`FilterExtended Yes` in
# tinyproxy.conf), matched against the request's host only (`FilterURLs No`).
# Everything not matching a pattern here is refused (`FilterDefaultDeny Yes`).
#
# Every pattern MUST be anchored with `^...$` and have its dots escaped
# (`\.`). An unanchored pattern like `pypi.org` (tinyproxy's old `FilterType
# fqdn` substring mode, no longer used -- see tinyproxy.conf) would also match
# `pypi.org.evil.tld` or `evil-pypi.org.example.com`: substring/prefix
# matching on a hostname is not the same thing as matching that exact
# hostname, and the whole point of this allowlist is that a compromised
# sandbox can reach ONLY the two kinds of destination below (final draft
# §12.2 M8) -- not anything that merely contains their name.
#
# Keep this list to exactly two kinds of destination: the LLM gateway, and a
# package mirror for dependency installs. Add your real hostnames before
# deploying.

# The LLM gateway (LiteLLM). This is the Compose SERVICE NAME (`litellm` in
# docker-compose.yml), not a made-up internal domain -- sandboxes resolve it
# via Docker's embedded DNS on whatever network reaches this proxy.
^litellm$

# Package mirrors used by sandboxed builds and tests. Trim this to whatever
# your products actually need — every extra entry widens the blast radius of
# a compromised sandbox.
^pypi\.org$
^files\.pythonhosted\.org$
^registry\.npmjs\.org$
